,{"parameters":[{"name":"id","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}]},{"name":"halign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}]}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}]}]},{"name":"smufl","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Specifies the exact segno glyph to use.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc: